# @CMD@ manifest — the single source of truth for where each skill is linked.
#
# One skill per line, whitespace-separated:
#
#   <scope>              <name>          <source-dir>
#
# For example (uncomment to try, or run `@CMD@ add <dir>` and let the CLI write it):
#
#   user                 code-review     ~/skills/code-review
#   project:~/Code/api   deploy          ~/skills/deploy
#
# scope
#   user                 link into every agent on this machine: ~/.claude/skills,
#                        ~/.codex/skills, ~/.agents/skills — whichever exist
#   project:<repo>       link into <repo>/.claude/skills and <repo>/.codex/skills
#
# name                   what the agent sees. Keep it equal to the `name:` in the
#                        source SKILL.md frontmatter — `@CMD@ doctor` checks that.
#
# source-dir             the one real copy of the skill; must contain SKILL.md.
#                        `~` expands to your home directory. No spaces in the path.
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored, and a # comment may also
# follow an entry.
#
# After editing this file by hand, reconcile the links:  @CMD@ sync
# Or let the CLI do both at once:                        @CMD@ edit
